[start-outcomes] After this part you should be able to
1. explain why an unbraced frame under lateral load has points of contraflexure near the mid-height of its columns and the mid-span of its beams, and which assumption each approximate method adds;
2. analyse a frame storey by storey by the cantilever method: the column axial forces, the beam and column shears, and the bending moments;
3. analyse a frame by the portal method: the storey shear shared by the spans, the beam moments joint by joint, and the column axial forces;
4. combine the wind moments with the vertical-load moments at a level by the course method (BS 8110 load combination 3), for both wind directions, with the reversal of a beam end;
5. compare the cantilever and portal methods, and the course method with the EN 1990 combinations and the EC2 imperfections.
